<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $63.3 mln Oct 14.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $63.3 mln Oct 14.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $63.3 million surplus on October 14 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 14</p>
<p>Exports: $184.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $165.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $172.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $128.3 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $63.3 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.634 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.411 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.439 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.574 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.088 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
